(2283760, 310602, 3032, '<td valign="top">In reply to your forum question:<br/> <br/>I scored this a six. <br/>Not lower, because I like the concept, the way the swan is lit and the ambiance of the photo.<br/>Not higher because composition wise it is too centered and too 2D. For a strong composition you should try to get some diagonals or triangle lines (not like put a straight line in it, but lines of sight) in your shot. This is a bit to head on for me.<br/> <br/></td>', 'In reply to your forum question: I scored this a six. Not lower, because I like the concept, the way the swan is lit and the ambiance of the photo.Not higher because composition wise it is too centered and too 2D. For a strong composition you should try to get some diagonals or triangle lines (not like put a straight line in it, but lines of sight) in your shot. This is a bit to head on for me. ', '2006-04-03 14:19:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2283766, 312035, 38127, '<td valign="top">;) I was watching your posts in the Water thread and our scores were neck and neck for most of the voting period. I couldnt wait to find out which was yours ;)  (I feel good that I placed so close to you.. means i''m doing something right) <br/>This is a great shot, I love finding unique things out walking, or hiking around.. the perspective from which you shot it is awesome. It leaves enough to the imagination that people can form their own opinions about what is around or beyond to give it some mystery.  The colours are so vibrant too!! <br/> <br/>*what challenge are you entering in next? ;)*<br/> <br/></td>', ';) I was watching your posts in the Water thread and our scores were neck and neck for most of the voting period. I couldnt wait to find out which was yours ;)  (I feel good that I placed so close to you.. means i''m doing something right) This is a great shot, I love finding unique things out walking, or hiking around.. the perspective from which you shot it is awesome. It leaves enough to the imagination that people can form their own opinions about what is around or beyond to give it some mystery.  The colours are so vibrant too!!  *what challenge are you entering in next? ;)* ', '2006-04-03 14:21:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2283786, 309085, 19672, '<td valign="top">I gave you a three, and here''s why...<br/> <br/>I thought the idea was fantastic, and their are aspects I really liked.  The swirls, texture, etc.<br/> <br/>That said, there was a feeling of blurriness that made it hard to focus. And was compounded by a lack of subject. I found myself peering out of a window of ice only to see what...a tree trunk. <br/> <br/>Had it peered out to a tree branch with a bird? or perhaps to see a flower budding up out of the ground. Or even the sun thru the tree branches. If there was a strong subject to catch my eye upon peering thru, then this shot would have received a good solid 6+ from me.<br/> <br/>- Saj</td>', 'I gave you a three, and here''s why... I thought the idea was fantastic, and their are aspects I really liked.  The swirls, texture, etc. That said, there was a feeling of blurriness that made it hard to focus. And was compounded by a lack of subject. I found myself peering out of a window of ice only to see what...a tree trunk.  Had it peered out to a tree branch with a bird? or perhaps to see a flower budding up out of the ground. Or even the sun thru the tree branches. If there was a strong subject to catch my eye upon peering thru, then this shot would have received a good solid 6+ from me. - Saj', '2006-04-03 14:29:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2283817, 312206, 22689, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot ! I gave it 8 , glad to know it''s yours !<br/>I like colors a lot : a good mix with rusty tones , greens and blues.<br/>The only detail I would take off is a sort of red strip or ribbon in the bottom left-hand corner.<br/></td>', 'Very nice shot ! I gave it 8 , glad to know it''s yours !I like colors a lot : a good mix with rusty tones , greens and blues.The only detail I would take off is a sort of red strip or ribbon in the bottom left-hand corner.', '2006-04-03 14:39:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2283822, 310101, 16046, '<td valign="top">Kudos on your "home run" Bear, I''m sure you''ll have many more.<br/>Frank</td>', 'Kudos on your "home run" Bear, I''m sure you''ll have many more.Frank', '2006-04-03 14:44:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2283906, 311229, 52336, '<td valign="top">In response to your <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=372338" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">request for comment</a>:  Overall, I think this is a good photograph, with an interesting composition and beautiful subject matter.  It''s probably not a <i>great</i> photograph despite it''s beauty, and I can only really offer my opinion on why that may be.  First, as someone noted, it lacks a subject, because we have the interesting horizon with its lighthouse, the dramatic swirling water (which could be the real subject of the image), and the nice red rocks.  It''s all nice, but a tighter focus on one particular element may have helped, which is odd, because many fine landscapes are made from multiple elements.  Perhaps more focus on the churning water would have been of greatest interest - you could then have really focused the detail, tried some impressive post work, and truly satisfied the challenge.<br/> <br/>The image itself is a bit soft, which may really detract from a landscape with so many elements.  More sharpening, and some noise reduction to get rid of the grain in the nice blue sky, could have enhanced the picture.  Also, if we are meant to look at all the elements, the lack of detail in the land at the horizon defeats the purpose.  The rock element at left is quite chopped off, and for me, weights the picture on that side none too pleasantly.  My eye keeps wandering there, so is that the subject?  It''s not clear to me.<br/> <br/>My choice may have been to focus primarily on the water, and ensure that I got a very dramatic, detailed shot of the churning and waves created by the rocks.  I may have post-processed to bring out this detail.<br/> <br/>I hope this has helped, and thanks for asking for the comment.</td>', 'In response to your request for comment:  Overall, I think this is a good photograph, with an interesting composition and beautiful subject matter.  It''s probably not a great photograph despite it''s beauty, and I can only really offer my opinion on why that may be.  First, as someone noted, it lacks a subject, because we have the interesting horizon with its lighthouse, the dramatic swirling water (which could be the real subject of the image), and the nice red rocks.  It''s all nice, but a tighter focus on one particular element may have helped, which is odd, because many fine landscapes are made from multiple elements.  Perhaps more focus on the churning water would have been of greatest interest - you could then have really focused the detail, tried some impressive post work, and truly satisfied the challenge. The image itself is a bit soft, which may really detract from a landscape with so many elements.  More sharpening, and some noise reduction to get rid of the grain in the nice blue sky, could have enhanced the picture.  Also, if we are meant to look at all the elements, the lack of detail in the land at the horizon defeats the purpose.  The rock element at left is quite chopped off, and for me, weights the picture on that side none too pleasantly.  My eye keeps wandering there, so is that the subject?  It''s not clear to me. My choice may have been to focus primarily on the water, and ensure that I got a very dramatic, detailed shot of the churning and waves created by the rocks.  I may have post-processed to bring out this detail. I hope this has helped, and thanks for asking for the comment.', '2006-04-03 15:10:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2283946, 310101, 18552, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on another ribbon, Bear - this is such a lovely, lovely picture. I''m glad it won the blue!</td>', 'Congratulations on another ribbon, Bear - this is such a lovely, lovely picture. I''m glad it won the blue!', '2006-04-03 15:26:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2283953, 311623, 50695, '<td valign="top">I was your only 10! :) It''s rare that I don''t comment on a 10, but I wasn''t sure what to say. It''s simply a beautiful shot. I would say that it looks like a pen and ink drawing, and has some of the characteristics of a good pen and ink, but also some great textures like you might see in a charcoal drawing. I like how the strong lines divide this picture into sections, and each section seems to have something different to say. Also, you caught the bird perfectly, you lucky so-and-so! ;) But luck is the residue of skill (and hard work), of course.</td>', 'I was your only 10! :) It''s rare that I don''t comment on a 10, but I wasn''t sure what to say. It''s simply a beautiful shot. I would say that it looks like a pen and ink drawing, and has some of the characteristics of a good pen and ink, but also some great textures like you might see in a charcoal drawing. I like how the strong lines divide this picture into sections, and each section seems to have something different to say. Also, you caught the bird perfectly, you lucky so-and-so! ;) But luck is the residue of skill (and hard work), of course.', '2006-04-03 15:28:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2283959, 310101, 5792, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your 1st blue. Many more are sure to come!</td>', 'Congrats on your 1st blue. Many more are sure to come!', '2006-04-03 15:31:05.000000', NULL, 0),
